        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="box_hop7_desc" value="HOP 7 DESIGN (PD-085, Case Point 3):&#10;Target: 60 s. Mobile network delivery to farmer's phone.&#10;Total Budget Sum: 210 s  |  Safety Margin: 90 s  |  Case Limit: 300 s (&lt;5 minutes)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ecfdf5;strokeColor=#059669;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#065f46;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3150" y="1515" width="480" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_table_box" value="CROP ALERT LATENCY BUDGET TABLE (docs/connectivity.md Section 8.2):&#10;&#10;Hop 1: Reading taken to message ready on node           Target:  10 s  | Cumulative:  10 s  | Node publishes immediately; no local evaluation&#10;Hop 2: Radio wake, network attach and TLS connection    Target:  60 s  | Cumulative:  70 s  | Multi-network SIM attaches to best available carrier&#10;Hop 3: MQTT publish to PUBACK at IoT Core endpoint      Target:  20 s  | Cumulative:  90 s  | QoS 1 with PUBACK; absorbs transient retransmissions&#10;Hop 4: Topic rule to threshold function invocation       Target:  10 s  | Cumulative: 100 s  | Routing rule through SQS threshold queue&#10;Hop 5: Threshold function evaluation &amp; persistence      Target:  20 s  | Cumulative: 120 s  | Evaluates ranges, persists DynamoDB, dispatches SNS&#10;Hop 6: Alert topic to notification channel provider     Target:  30 s  | Cumulative: 150 s  | Amazon SNS HTTPS dispatch to Push/SMS gateway&#10;Hop 7: Channel provider to farmer's smartphone          Target:  60 s  | Cumulative: 210 s  | Push notification or SMS delivered to farmer phone&#10;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&#10;Total Design Target: 210 s (3.5 min)  |  Safety Margin: 90 s  |  Case Statement Hard Limit: 300 s (&lt;5 minutes, Case Point 3)" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#475569;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#0f172a;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1880" y="1590" width="1760" height="240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2_slo_box" value="TRACEABILITY TO A21 ALERT-DELIVERY SLO (docs/connectivity.md Section 8.3 &amp; Roadmap #34):&#10;- Proposed SLI: Share of out-of-range readings published live (not from buffer) whose notification arrives on farmer phone within 300 s.&#10;- Trace Points: 1. Reading timestamp (Hop 1) | 2. Broker PUBACK (Hop 3) | 3. Lambda execution start &amp; alert persist (Hop 5) | 4. SNS handoff (Hop 6) | 5. Delivery receipt (Hop 7).&#10;- Hop timestamps allow A21 to attribute any SLO breach to the exact failing hop (field attach vs cloud queue vs carrier SMS).&#10;- Drained readings (offline buffer) are measured separately against the 24-hour limit; drying alerts use the identical budget." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#eff6ff;strokeColor=#2563eb;strokeWidth=1.5;fontColor=#1e40af;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1880" y="1850" width="1760" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="seq_global_note" value="DIAGRAM METADATA &amp; NORMATIVE RULES: Part of ALPH-20 / ALPH-23. Repository aroma-pacifico-diagrams (network/). Refs aroma-pacifico/aroma-pacifico-roadmap#19. Closes ALPH-23.&#10;All timings and latencies are design targets defined in docs/connectivity.md. Diagram adheres to zero-emoji policy and strict Draw.io XML standards." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f1f5f9;strokeColor=#64748b;strokeWidth=1;fontColor=#334155;fontSize=12;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="2180" width="3620" height="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>